#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
r"""
HTA Bridge 2  -  extract, document and drive the Hybrid Test Application (HTA)
==============================================================================

WHAT IT DOES
------------
1. EXTRACT    every HTA widget (tab, name, type, min/max, step, unit, button
              states, model path, position, size) into an Excel workbook -
              one sheet per HTA tab + index + "Sequence" sheet.
              Sources: layout/view-set XML files, live scan of the running HTA
              (UI Automation), or HTA's "Change Widget Properties" dialogs.
2. KEYWORDS   every widget gets a unique 3-5 letter keyword, stored in
              Keywords.xlsx:  All Wheel Speeds -> AWS, Ignition OnOff -> IGN,
              KL30A V -> KLA, PAU Mode #2 -> PAUMB ...  Families such as
              fl/fr/rl/rr_tractor_kmh also get one GROUP keyword, and you can add
              MACRO keywords ("BAT" = "KLA$; KLB$").  Edit the file, press Refresh.
3. CONSOLE    command prompt in the GUI (and CLI):  AWS100   IGN ON   KLA?
              KLA+=0.5   AWSMAX   PUP!   START   STOP   RESET   KEYS kl30   HELP
4. CONTROL    GUI with one table per HTA tab: type values, Apply -> written
              into HTA (range-checked, read back, audit-logged, undo, dry run).
5. SIMULATION Start / Stop / Reset HTA from the toolbar (F9 / F10 / Ctrl+F9).
6. HARDWARE   "Channels / Hardware": open any HTA menu dialog, capture its
              fields, set values, apply + OK; profiles saved in HTA_Config.xlsx.
7. AUTOMATE   SET / CHECK / WAIT / WAIT_UNTIL / PRESS / READ / PAUSE steps from
              the Sequence sheet -> PASS/FAIL Excel report.

INSTALL  (Windows 10/11, Python 3.7 - 3.13)
-------------------------------------------
    python hta_bridge.py install          (or the "Libs" button in the GUI;
                                            a setup window appears automatically
                                            if the GUI libraries are missing)
    Python 3.7: pip picks the last versions that support it automatically
    (PySide6 6.5.x, openpyxl 3.1.3, lxml 5.x) - nothing extra to do.

QUICK START
-----------
    python hta_bridge.py demo                     # offline demo (simulated HTA)
    python hta_bridge.py find-layouts             # locate HTA layout XML files
    python hta_bridge.py extract --xml "C:\HTA\Layouts" --live -o HTA_Signals.xlsx
    python hta_bridge.py gui HTA_Signals.xlsx     # GUI -> F2 = connect HTA
    python hta_bridge.py console HTA_Signals.xlsx # keyword prompt without GUI
    python hta_bridge.py cmd HTA_Signals.xlsx "KLA24; IGN ON" "AWS100"
    python hta_bridge.py sim start|stop|reset|status
    python hta_bridge.py menus                    # list HTA menu entries
    python hta_bridge.py config capture --menu "Settings -> Hardware..." --name Bench3
    python hta_bridge.py config apply --name Bench3
    python hta_bridge.py keywords HTA_Signals.xlsx  # create / update Keywords.xlsx
    python hta_bridge.py apply HTA_Signals.xlsx   # push every 'Set Value' cell
    python hta_bridge.py run HTA_Signals.xlsx     # run the Sequence sheet
    python hta_bridge.py inspect                  # dump HTA control tree (support)
    python hta_bridge.py selftest                 # built-in test suite

LARGE HTAs (10 000+ widgets)
----------------------------
Extraction runs as its own process, Excel/keyword work runs in a helper process,
tab tables are built only when opened, and the live scan reads a whole tab in
one UI-Automation request - the window stays responsive while all of this runs.
Excel files are written by streaming the data rows straight into the sheet XML
(openpyxl still writes headers, colours, drop-downs, filters), and saving values
patches only the touched cells in place - formatting and other sheets untouched.
Every fast path checks itself and falls back to plain openpyxl automatically.

HOW VALUES REACH HTA
--------------------
HTA is driven exactly like an operator would drive it, through Windows UI
Automation (pywinauto): select the tab, locate the widget (automation id ->
caption label -> XML position), type the value + Enter (or use the UIA
Value/RangeValue pattern), click toggle buttons until they show the wanted
state, read the control back to verify.  Simulation Start/Stop/Reset use HTA's
toolbar buttons (menu fallback); dialogs are opened through HTA's own menus.

All files the tool creates live in  %USERPROFILE%\HTA_Bridge  (settings, logs,
audit trail, sequence reports) unless configured otherwise; Keywords.xlsx and
HTA_Config.xlsx are kept next to the signal workbook.
"""
